    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "`search_remote` is now implemented in `kb/remote.py`. It connects over Streamable HTTP, sends `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on every request, calls the `search` tool and turns the result into titles with the same `split_titles` helper that `search_local` uses.\n\n```python\nasync def search_remote(url: str, token: str, query: str) -> list[str]:\n    headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"}\n    async with httpx2.AsyncClient(headers=headers, timeout=TIMEOUT) as http_client:\n        async with streamable_http_client(url, http_client=http_client) as (read, write):\n            async with ClientSession(read, write) as session:\n                await session.initialize()\n                result = await session.call_tool(\"search\", {\"query\": query})\n    return split_titles(result)\n```\n\n**Differences from older MCP SDKs.** I read the pinned `mcp==2.2.0` source directly rather than going by older docs, because this version differs in three ways:\n- `streamable_http_client` gives back two streams, not three.\n- It uses `httpx2`, not `httpx`. `httpx2` is already a dependency of `mcp`, so nothing was added to `pyproject.toml`.\n- You set headers by passing your own HTTP client. The SDK's helper for building that client is private, so I create the client directly with the same timeouts (30s, and 300s for reads). The SDK doesn't close a client you pass in, so the code closes it.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `pytest -q` passes (2 tests).\n- I also ran it against a local MCP server that rejects any request without `Bearer s3cret`. The call returned `['Rotating API keys', 'Onboarding']`, and all 6 requests carried the token: the POSTs, the background GET stream and the DELETE sent when the session closes.\n\n**One thing to do:** I couldn't delete the scratch check script `_check_remote.py` in the project root because the removal needed approval. Please delete it, or approve the removal and I'll do it. pytest doesn't pick it up, since tests only run from `tests/`."
